{"title":"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Of the following five statements, I to V, about the binary operation of averaging (arithmetic mean), \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/f/2bf68f2cae7fb8f152cb0c5917c2fdbcddd61fac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{I. Averaging is associative }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"188\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/3/c93f80f916472c36b5279cdfc650bef5a1cec536.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{II. Averaging is commutative }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"211\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/3/b23b1506366a3950aaacfaada24e4dc054fbb503.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{III. Averaging distributes over addition }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"285\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/7/79717003c7afebfe184be707129a73bbe0371b4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{IV. Addition distributes over averaging }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"285\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/3/2d3fa9d7f32ee2f9fa21acb1acc7a9e213cfb59e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{V. Averaging has an identity element }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"279\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>those which are always true are \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/7/97700720d702ef3b85f652d255bac9ce55bc878e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\text{All}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\text{I and II only}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\text{II and III only}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"389\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/7/8178bfe7cb098ec01ca25c11a361371397773e5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{II and IV only}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{II and V only}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"305\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can consider each statement independently and see which ones are true. The average of two numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/2/eb2043001aea9e5f205ff266b49cc66b9d06b887.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$avg(x, y) = \\frac{x + y}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"139\" height=\"35\" />.\n</p><p><b>Statement I</b>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/6/046e5038428a07d23e9329a6bd3375ca8fb1edd6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[avg(avg(x, y), z) = avg(x, avg(y, z))\\]\" width=\"283\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/5/fb5d2fb2745e6e7d41d7970c6ed0075cdc18a28b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\frac{x + y}{2} + z}{2} = \\frac{x + \\frac{y + z}{2}}{2}\\]\" width=\"149\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/1/1f161c97849821602c2b23dba5eacc6b9e2a08da.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x + y + 2z}{4} = \\frac{2x + y + z}{4}\\]\" width=\"194\" height=\"37\" />\nThe above statement is not true for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/b/31b1e1af4531148cbc079023f68c2b0102c4ee69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, y, z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"61\" height=\"20\" />, so Statement I is false.\n</p><p><br />\n<b>Statement II</b>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/3/4134752a2e2e2bb81fbcdf674b12f946fe33d0e4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[avg(x, y) = avg(y, x)\\]\" width=\"163\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/0/5f0ac97e4ac91f60e16085e045cc9e94b9404f40.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x + y}{2} = \\frac{y + x}{2}\\]\" width=\"113\" height=\"35\" />\nSince addition is commutative, the above is true for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" />, so Statement II is true.\n</p><p><br />\n<b>Statement III</b>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/4/644ebb5860a12e5266e613609a7929099a4ae9b9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[avg(x, y + z) = avg(x, y) + avg(x, z)\\]\" width=\"287\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/2/d02ecedf5ea566b4aca6827e8125cf67ee33f417.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x + y + z}{2} = \\frac{x + y}{2} + \\frac{x + z}{2}\\]\" width=\"212\" height=\"35\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/e/36e4fded44b53d05d7831a115c0edbff1d16bc89.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x + y + z}{2} = \\frac{2x + y + z}{2}\\]\" width=\"185\" height=\"37\" />\nThe above statement is not true for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/b/31b1e1af4531148cbc079023f68c2b0102c4ee69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, y, z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"61\" height=\"20\" />, so Statement III is false.\n</p><p><br />\n<b>Statement IV</b>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/b/39b5ff4c7fd1fa45e35393dae5f4a10d0f0c7b90.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x + avg(y, z) = avg(x + y, x + z)\\]\" width=\"259\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/7/c074802588d2a157776e99441e97e2a59e255fda.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x + \\frac{y + z}{2} = \\frac{2x + y + z}{2}\\]\" width=\"186\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/5/375fca6fcc67e29a23b33b7914a42704ef9e1503.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{2x + y + z}{2} = \\frac{2x + y + z}{2}\\]\" width=\"194\" height=\"37\" />\nThe left side and the right side are equivalent expressions, so Statement IV is true.\n</p><p><br />\n<b>Statement V</b>\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> be the identity element. If such <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> exists, then the following is true:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/0/700a9259995c04f5b861fb51a2bb7e6abbbd8b73.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[avg(x, i) = x\\]\" width=\"101\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/9/359a63a8fbd8e4609f7d87a64d2ebcefd580fb2b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x + i}{2} = x\\]\" width=\"75\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67b027c251b9603cae3d1c77388475c7974387ea.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x + i = 2x\\]\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/0/6503d672fc84b5e162728772b28ad4f77be93c29.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[i = x\\]\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />\nHowever, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is a variable, but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> must be a constant, fixed number, there is no identity element for the binary operation of averaging. Therefore, Statement V is false.\n</p><p>Statements II and IV are true, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/0/8909e383b947364af34124c9c321d72feb87e40a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)} \\text{II and IV only}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"146\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME\" title=\"1973 AHSME\">1973 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1973 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1973\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1973 AHSM